/-!
# Exchange-certificate data: `E8` seeds

The seeds of the `E8` exchange-certificate data; its variables, exchange relations, cover
tree and raw certificate are in `CertificateData.E8`. Each seed is one natural number whose
bit fields hold its cluster, its matrix digits, its transitions, their relabellings and
relations, and its position in a breadth-first spanning tree. The definition is
`noncomputable`: only the kernel evaluates it.

## Implementation notes

The lookup tree is assembled here from its top 5 levels and the subtrees
`seedPart0` to `seedPart31` below them, each defined in a file
`CertificateData.E8SeedsPart*`, so that no one file holds the whole tree.
-/

